+# Penetration Test Plan (PoC)
+
+Objective:
+- Identify security weaknesses in IdP, secrets handling, qpu-worker, queue, webhooks and device interfaces.
+
+Scope:
+- Keycloak realm & clients (token issuance, scopes, role mapping)
+- K8s RBAC and ServiceAccount IRSA bindings
+- Secrets Manager & KMS access from pods (IRSA roles)
+- QPU queue endpoints and worker processes
+- Webhooks (mutating/validating) TLS, CA rotation and RBAC
+- Device enrollment API and device agent flows (OTA, telemetry)
+
+Tests:
+1. Auth & token tests:
+ - Attempt to call control endpoints without tokens, with expired tokens, and with insufficient scopes.
+2. Secrets access:
+ - Validate least-privilege IAM: can qpu-worker SA only read assigned secrets?
+3. Webhook TLS:
+ - Ensure CA rotation attacker cannot inject webhook; test with rotated CA bundles.
+4. QPU provider abuse:
+ - Ensure queue cannot be used to exfiltrate secrets (payload validation).
+5. Device attack surface:
+ - Attempt to enroll device with forged CSR; test CRL enforcement and revocation.
+
+Reporting:
+- Capture all findings in the repository under docs/security-findings/ and upload signed evidence to evidence S3.
+
